@module flutter-m07 | Forms and User Input
@summary Collect and validate input with controllers, focus, pickers and selection controls.

@lesson flutter-m07-l01 | TextEditingController | 8
## Learning objectives
- Read and set text field values

## TextEditingController
A `TextEditingController` gives you the current text, selection and a way to set or clear text. Create it in initState and dispose it in dispose.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

class Search extends StatefulWidget {
  const Search({super.key});
  @override
  State<Search> createState() => _SearchState();
}

class _SearchState extends State<Search> {
  final _controller = TextEditingController();
  @override
  void dispose() { _controller.dispose(); super.dispose(); }
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) => TextField(
        controller: _controller,
        decoration: InputDecoration(suffixIcon: IconButton(icon: const Icon(Icons.clear), onPressed: _controller.clear)),
      );
}
```

## Summary
- Controllers read/write field text.
- Always dispose them.

@lesson flutter-m07-l02 | Form widgets | 8
## Learning objectives
- Group fields with Form and TextFormField

## Form widgets
`Form` coordinates validation, saving and resetting of its `FormField` descendants such as `TextFormField`.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

final key = GlobalKey<FormState>();
String? name;

Widget form() => Form(
      key: key,
      child: TextFormField(onSaved: (v) => name = v, decoration: const InputDecoration(labelText: 'Name')),
    );

void submit() { if (key.currentState!.validate()) key.currentState!.save(); }
```

## Summary
- Form groups fields.
- validate() then save().

@lesson flutter-m07-l03 | Validators | 8
## Learning objectives
- Write reusable validation functions

## Validators
Validators are functions returning an error message or null. Compose them for reuse and show messages as soon as useful with `autovalidateMode: AutovalidateMode.onUserInteraction`.

```dart
String? requiredField(String? v) => (v == null || v.trim().isEmpty) ? 'Required' : null;

String? email(String? v) {
  final e = requiredField(v);
  if (e != null) return e;
  return RegExp(r'^[^@\s]+@[^@\s]+\.[^@\s]+$').hasMatch(v!) ? null : 'Enter a valid email';
}
```

## Summary
- Return null for valid input.
- Validate on user interaction for fast feedback.

@lesson flutter-m07-l04 | Focus management | 8
## Learning objectives
- Move focus between fields

## Focus management
`FocusNode` controls keyboard focus. With `textInputAction: TextInputAction.next`, fields move focus automatically; call `FocusScope.of(context).unfocus()` to hide the keyboard.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

Widget fields() => const Column(children: [
      TextField(textInputAction: TextInputAction.next, decoration: InputDecoration(labelText: 'Email')),
      TextField(textInputAction: TextInputAction.done, obscureText: true, decoration: InputDecoration(labelText: 'Password')),
    ]);
```

## Summary
- TextInputAction.next moves focus.
- Dispose FocusNodes you create.

@lesson flutter-m07-l05 | Keyboard handling | 8
## Learning objectives
- Keep fields visible when the keyboard opens

## Keyboard handling
Scaffold resizes when the keyboard appears. Put forms in a scroll view so fields can scroll into view, and dismiss the keyboard when tapping outside.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

Widget page(Widget form) => Scaffold(
      body: GestureDetector(
        onTap: () => FocusManager.instance.primaryFocus?.unfocus(),
        child: SingleChildScrollView(padding: const EdgeInsets.all(16), child: form),
      ),
    );
```

## Summary
- Wrap forms in a scroll view.
- Tap outside to unfocus.

@lesson flutter-m07-l06 | Checkboxes | 8
## Learning objectives
- Toggle boolean options

## Checkboxes
`Checkbox` and `CheckboxListTile` toggle a bool. ListTile variants make the whole row tappable and accessible.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

Widget terms(bool value, ValueChanged<bool?> onChanged) => CheckboxListTile(
      value: value,
      onChanged: onChanged,
      title: const Text('I accept the terms'),
    );
```

## Summary
- Prefer CheckboxListTile for labelled options.

@lesson flutter-m07-l07 | Radio buttons | 8
## Learning objectives
- Choose one option from a set

## Radio buttons
Radio buttons select exactly one option. `RadioListTile<T>` shows a labelled choice; all tiles share a `groupValue`.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

enum Level { beginner, advanced }

Widget levels(Level group, ValueChanged<Level?> onChanged) => Column(children: [
      for (final l in Level.values)
        RadioListTile<Level>(value: l, groupValue: group, onChanged: onChanged, title: Text(l.name)),
    ]);
```

## Summary
- Use radios for a single choice among few options.

@lesson flutter-m07-l08 | Switches | 8
## Learning objectives
- Turn settings on and off

## Switches
Switches toggle settings that take effect immediately. Use `SwitchListTile` with a title and optional subtitle.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

Widget darkMode(bool on, ValueChanged<bool> onChanged) =>
    SwitchListTile(value: on, onChanged: onChanged, title: const Text('Dark mode'));
```

## Summary
- Switches apply immediately; checkboxes often need a submit.

@lesson flutter-m07-l09 | Sliders | 8
## Learning objectives
- Pick a value from a range

## Sliders
`Slider` selects a value within min/max; `divisions` makes it discrete and `label` shows the current value.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

Widget fontSize(double value, ValueChanged<double> onChanged) => Slider(
      value: value, min: 12, max: 24, divisions: 6, label: value.round().toString(), onChanged: onChanged,
    );
```

## Summary
- Use divisions for discrete steps.
- RangeSlider selects a range.

@lesson flutter-m07-l10 | Dropdowns | 8
## Learning objectives
- Pick from a list of options

## Dropdowns
`DropdownMenu<T>` (Material 3) shows a text field with a menu of entries; `DropdownButtonFormField` integrates with forms.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

Widget country(ValueChanged<String?> onSelected) => DropdownMenu<String>(
      label: const Text('Country'),
      onSelected: onSelected,
      dropdownMenuEntries: const [
        DropdownMenuEntry(value: 'PT', label: 'Portugal'),
        DropdownMenuEntry(value: 'IN', label: 'India'),
      ],
    );
```

## Summary
- DropdownMenu is the M3 dropdown.

@lesson flutter-m07-l11 | Date and time pickers | 8
## Learning objectives
- Let users pick dates and times

## Date and time pickers
`showDatePicker` and `showTimePicker` open Material dialogs and return the selection (or null if cancelled).

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

Future<void> pick(BuildContext context) async {
  final date = await showDatePicker(context: context, firstDate: DateTime(2020), lastDate: DateTime(2030), initialDate: DateTime.now());
  if (date == null || !context.mounted) return;
  final time = await showTimePicker(context: context, initialTime: TimeOfDay.now());
  debugPrint('$date $time');
}
```

## Summary
- Pickers return null when cancelled.
- Check context.mounted after await.
